Article 12
(1) Empowerment of Women victims of acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination shall be carried out in an integrated manner in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(2) Empowerment of Women victims of acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be directed to obtain opportunities and rights as human beings in order to be able to play a role and participate in activities:
a. health;
b. education;
c. economy;
d. law;
e. employment;
f. politics;
g. government;
h. social;
i. culture; and
j. living environment.

CHAPTER VII
PARTICIPATION
Article 30
(1) Every person may participate in the implementation of Women's Protection in the Region.
(2) Participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by individuals, groups as well as social community organizations, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, Law Enforcement Institutions, service institutions, religious institutions, Islamic boarding schools, professional organizations, legal aid organizations, youth organizations, broadcasting supervisory institutions, media, communities, professional institutions, business sector as well as other related stakeholders.
(3) Participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may take the form of:
a. providing information or reporting to the competent authority if aware of acts of violence, and/or exploitation and/or discrimination against women;
b. taking preventive action against violence against women;
c. conducting professional skills training in the form of:
1. leadership training;
2. management training;
3. business communication training;
4. negotiation skills training;
5. technology and digital training; and
6. entrepreneurship training;
d. conducting specific skills training in the form of:
1. self-defense training;
2. creative arts skills training; and
3. handicrafts, cooking skills, sewing skills, child care skills, and household management skills;
e. conducting health and welfare training in the form of:
1. fitness training; and
2. mental health training;
f. conducting community and social training in the form of:
1. activism and advocacy training; and
2. volunteer training in various social, health, and environmental fields;
g. establishing social community institutions that handle the guidance and empowerment of women.
(4) Further provisions regarding community participation as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be regulated in a Mayor Regulation.

CHAPTER V
INSTITUTIONAL ARRANGEMENTS
Article 26
(1) The Regional Government in its efforts to provide and administer protection services for women victims of violence, exploitation and acts of violence shall establish UPTD PPA.
(2) UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be under and responsible to the head of the Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.
(3) UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (2) shall have the duties to:
 a. receive reports or conduct outreach to Victims;
 b. provide information about the rights of Victims;
 c. facilitate the provision of health services;
 d. facilitate the provision of psychological strengthening services;
 e. facilitate the provision of psychosocial services, social rehabilitation, social empowerment, and social reintegration;
 f. provide legal services;
 g. identify economic empowerment needs;
 h. identify temporary shelter needs for Victims and Victims' Families that need to be fulfilled immediately;
 i. facilitate the needs of Victims with Disabilities;
 j. coordinate and work together on the fulfillment of Victims' rights with other institutions; and
 k. monitor the fulfillment of Victims' rights by law enforcement apparatus during the judicial process.
(4) UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be grouped into roles as follows:
 a. health;
 b. psychology;
 c. social-education;
 d. law; and
 e. economy.
(5) Further provisions regarding the establishment, main duties and functions as well as management of UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by a Mayor Regulation.

MAYOR OF SURAKARTA
CENTRAL JAVA PROVINCE
REGIONAL REGULATION OF SURAKARTA CITY NUMBER 7 OF 2024
CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF WOMEN
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD THE MAYOR OF SURAKARTA,
COPY
Considering : a. that women are citizens who have human rights that must be protected, respected, maintained, and may not be ignored, reduced, or seized by anyone, thus requiring guaranteed protection from acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination and need to be empowered so that they can actualize their potential optimally;
b. that in order to realize the fulfillment of women's constitutional rights to be free from acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination, as well as to improve the quality of life of women, they need to receive protection and empowerment from the Regional Government;
c. that the implementation of protection of women in the Region has not been able to be carried out optimally and is accompanied by the continued occurrence of acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women, thus requiring a comprehensive regulation to provide direction, foundation, and legal certainty;
- 2 -
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women;
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 16 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Large City Regions Within the Province of East Java, Central Java, West Java and the Special Region of Yogyakarta (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1950 Number 45);
3. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 6 of 2023 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2022 concerning Job Creation into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2023 Number 41, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6856);
4. Law Number 12 of 2022 concerning the Criminal Act of Sexual Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2022 Number 120, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6792);
5. Law Number 11 of 2023 concerning Central Java Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2023 Number 58 Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6867);
- 3 - With the Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF SURAKARTA CITY and

